+@section tonemap_vulkan
+
+Tone map HDR video to SDR using Vulkan.
+
+It accepts the following parameters:
+
+@table @option
+@item tonemap
+Specify the tone mapping algorithm to use.
+Only @code{bt2408_hable} is currently supported (default).
+
+@table @samp
+@item bt2408_hable
+ITU-R BT.2408 tone mapping with Hable curve on IPT intensity.
+@end table
+
+@item peak
+Signal peak override, in units of 100 cd/m^2 (nits / 100). Default is @code{0},
+which means the peak is determined from frame metadata.
+
+@item format
+Output software pixel format of the hardware frames. Can be @code{nv12} or
+@code{p010}. Default is @code{nv12}.
+@end table
+
+@subsection Example
+
+@itemize
+@item
+Tone map an HDR10 video to SDR NV12:
+@example
+ffmpeg -init_hw_device vulkan -filter_hw_device vulkan0 -i hdr10.mkv -vf "format=p010,hwupload,tonemap_vulkan,hwdownload,format=nv12" out
+@end example
+@end itemize
+
 @c man end VULKAN VIDEO FILTERS
 
 @chapter QSV Video Filters
